WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:09.700
Long pickup lines. Repeated classroom calls. Meet Driveline:
designed for coordinated arrivals, well-timed classroom calls,
and staff-confirmed handoffs.

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:23.104
Around half a mile, the approach zone prepares the app.
Near five hundred feet, arrival checks verify presence and
pickup rights. Schools configure these distances for their
campus.

3
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:31.700
Near school, the parent selects both children and checks in once.
Driveline verifies presence and pickup authorization.

4
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:38.966
The family joins the queue, and parents receive an arrival alert.
Children stay in class until the car is closer.

5
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.488
As the car moves forward, teachers receive the classroom call.
The hallway display shows the family's pickup tag.

6
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:55.700
At the curb, staff verify the authorized collector and confirm
the handoff, following the school's existing release procedure.

7
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:03.700
The completed pickup records the children, collector, and
confirming staff member. Parents receive a notification. A clear
journey home.
